<Base lang="en" title="Notes"><article class="prose"><p class="label">Traces</p><h1>Some things need not become a project first.</h1><div class="grid"><section class="card"><div><span class="number">CASE NOTES</span><h3>Case notes</h3><p>On systems, evidence, and the process of being recognized. Public notes retain only redacted facts, timelines, and shareable learning—never personal data, raw evidence, or details that could affect a process.</p></div></section><section class="card"><div><span class="number">TRACES</span><h3>Cats & everyday life</h3><p>Photos and small notes may arrive here later. For now it is simply a door; no photographs are used without being supplied and cleared for publication.</p></div></section></div><aside class="note">Case notes and cats have separate rooms here: one asks for accuracy; the other only asks to be remembered well.</aside></article></Base>
